      "corrected": "$E=7\\times10^{10}$",
      "reason": "Initial independent n50 SCI finding F1: the original aluminum modulus is 7 times 10^7 N/m^2. The rendered MIT 6.777J/2.751J material-property database gives the typical aluminum Young modulus as 70 GPa, equivalent to 7 times 10^10 N/m^2. Correct only this complete formula in the modern edition; do not assert a universal alloy/temperature value. Preserve every raw printed body/block, row, other equation, crop and source lesson snapshot. Reference: https://www.mit.edu/~6.777/matprops/aluminum.htm, read through CloakBrowser on 2026-11-16."
    }
